/* book exam traps: Entropy is a property: ΔS depends only on the end states, so never integrate δQ/T along an irreversible path; use a reversible substitute between the same states. | Put T in kelvin. Using Celsius in ln(T₂/T₁) gives a wrong number and can even make the log invalid. | Use cp for constant pressure and cv for constant volume; they are not interchangeable. | The area under a T-s path is heat only for a reversible path. For an irreversible process it is not the actual heat transfer. | S is extensive (kJ/K); s is per kg (kJ/kg·K). Do not mix them in the same formula. */
