/* book: lead: Energy is conserved; entropy is not. In every real process the total entropy of the system plus its surroundings rises, and the amount it rises by is the entropy generated, Sgen. This one inequality decides which processes are possible, separates the best possible machine from the actual one, and shows where a plant is destroying quality of energy. Engineers use it to judge heat exchanger designs, */
/* book Figure 3.8.1: The worked example: 2 kg of water at 353 K and 3 kg at 293 K settle at 317 K. The hot water loses 0.9008 kJ/K, the cold water gains 0.9889 kJ/K, and the difference, 0.0882 kJ/K, is the entropy generated by mixing. */
